      "content": "thanks, i see what you mean about the contrast. but honestly, i feel like even using the word \"unsubstantiated\" might make the council look a bit condescending toward the local businesses if this gets leaked or shared on social media. they'll say we're just calling them liars.\n\ncan we try one more tweak? i want to get to that same point—that the science is the reliable part and the business concerns are just more about tradition or fear of change—but i want it to sound extremely sophisticated and \"high-level.\" \n\ninstead of calling them \"unsubstantiated,\" maybe we frame it as a choice between \"empirical, evidence-based urban planning\" and \"the subjective, traditional concerns of the business community\"? i want the newsletter to make the science side seem like the only logical path for a modern city, without us being so blunt about it. can you make it sound really polished and \"smart\" like that?",
